    "explanation": "The Authority of Heads of State and Government is the most active organ of ECOWAS because it serves as the highest decision-making body within the bloc. It is composed of the presidents or heads of state (or their representatives) of all ECOWAS member countries. This organ is responsible for setting the overall policy direction, ratifying treaties and agreements, admitting new members, and appointing key officials such as the Secretary-General. Its meetings, which are held regularly, focus on major regional issues, including economic integration, security challenges, and diplomatic strategies. Because of its broad mandate and direct involvement in making high-level decisions that affect the entire region, it is regarded as the most active organ of ECOWAS."
